  "body": "## Problem and current execution state\n\nTwo surviving original C2 checkpoints now have independently verified cold-resume integrity (#6746). Their original controller remains UNKNOWN. This change freezes two separately identified, bounded CPU continuations so that further training can produce reviewable state, costs, and development metrics without rewriting the original incomplete execution.\n\n**This is a source/protocol and preparation-evidence Draft, not a completed-training report.** Native job `1a1f286aa59-ffbe-b5c`, unique identity `hcsn-c2-independent-continuation-20261119-d741-001`, was authoritatively observed RUNNING during publication preflight. No terminal training result is included or inferred here.\n\n## Frozen continuation\n\n- Resume `hcsn-s211-lr0.001` after complete epoch 126 and `hcsn-s307-lr0.001` after complete epoch 127, with full model, AdamW, Torch RNG, and episode-order RNG restoration.\n- Reuse the exact original v8 model and prepared train/development data. Physics and the shared frontend/head remain frozen; this is the original finite-grid QPR/remaining-time-phase model, not the new complete-state flow or endogenous-boundary control implementation.\n- Preserve the original strict-best and plateau definitions, minimum 30 cumulative epochs, patience 10, delta 0.002, and the inherited C2 cap of 200 complete epochs. The older parent plan's 100-epoch cap is explicitly distinguished in the request.\n- Retain actual batch/gradient/optimizer events, per-update and complete-epoch checkpoints, explicit partial-epoch cursors, and original full-D metrics. Confirmation E is not accessed. This does not claim completion of the old posterior/optimization-window recording contract.\n- The new CPU runtime is Python 3.12.3 / Torch 2.8.0+cpu / NumPy 2.3.5, not an exact replay of original Torch 2.8.0+cu128.\n\n## Bounded resources\n\nEach fit has a 6,000-second scientific wall budget, including imports, verification, training, evaluation, and finalization. A 300-second finalization reserve is inside that cap; 30 seconds of cleanup grace grants no additional scientific budget or qualification credit. There are two concurrent fits, one numerical thread per fit, pinned to distinct physical cores: two training CPUs total. Per fit, address space is limited to 8 GiB and the peak-RSS stop threshold is 6 GiB.\n\nThe original surviving partial tails (10 and 11 completed updates after the respective last complete checkpoints), unknown hidden/truncated tail work, and the four cold-probe calls remain separate work and cost. There is no work refund, original-key retry, or synthetic original terminal receipt.\n\n## Reviewable source and preparation evidence\n\nAll 90 additions are confined to `qualification/hcsn_c2_continuation_20261119/`. The final remote Git tree exactly equals local frozen commit `ff281e36f7e1a5480ca30ff3cf8a1efaac0114c6` (tree `e02c6a77c88e5a780ba2fe15e6905c0d455675d9`). Three reviewable commits separate the bounded input/process controller, the actual continuation runner, and retained preparation/lifecycle-control attempts.\n\nThe complete 1,068,867-byte `BINDINGS.json` is retained, SHA-256 `68cfdb6f30c7ce1b06e1f0f41f2f7b97c8404b6000e26e13cffc55bedc764070`. Its uploaded Git blob is `ce9bae6a95e190ce26c0b6373d4260cb32e56d6f`.\n\nEarlier preparation/control failures remain alongside the final synthetic controller check. The final control verifies distinct CPU assignment, successful child reaping, budget-stop signaling, and exact wait4 receipts; it makes zero C2/model calls and is not a training-quality test. The initial-checkpoint fallback uses an original same-seed alternate-learning-rate initial file only after matching the target fit's original admission byte length and full SHA exactly; missing original paths are not repaired.\n\nThe source owner ran `just fmt --base 12ac0f27b3babe6b00c275b6120096760dc78f87` from `codex-rs`: exit 0, no applicable formatter for these qualification paths, no byte changes. The exact base-to-source `git diff --check` also exits 0.\n\n## Publication isolation and unchanged claims\n\nThe exact base is #6746 head `f69d6c5845bec079ddafbc6a791ad70d012faf32` on `research/hcsn-c2-cold-resume-20261119-d741`; its tree equals the local source parent. The comparison has 90 added files, zero deletions, and no out-of-scope paths. No existing branch, source, checkpoint, or workflow is modified.\n\nThe inherited N256 one-shot workflow's PR-open path filters do not match this continuation directory. No workflow dispatch or new numerical run is initiated by publication.\n\n**Original controller UNKNOWN, full six-fit replay 0/6, and scientific admission HOLD remain unchanged.** Completion, training adequacy, development quality, and execution cost require the new terminal artifacts and their separate independent review.\n",
